In classic WoW, warlocks favor voidwalkers for **group content** (raids/dungeons) due to their **AoE taunt (Suffering)** and **threat generation**, which help manage enemy aggro. Succubi excel in **solo leveling/questing** with **single-target damage (Lash of Pain)**, **crowd control (Seduction)**, and **stealth (Lesser Invisibility)**. Voidwalkers’ **out-of-combat health regeneration (Consume Shadows)** also aids survival in sustained fights. Thus, voidwalkers are preferred for group scenarios, while succubi dominate solo play. [end of text]


